## The Bilinear Sum-Closure structural identity

For a bounded smooth stationary 3D NS solution `u : ℝ³ → ℝ³` with
Bohr-Fourier representation
   `u(x) = Σ_{ξ ∈ Σ} a_ξ e^{2πi ξ·x}`,   Σ ⊂ ℝ³ countable
divergence-free condition gives `ξ · a_ξ = 0` for all `ξ ∈ Σ`.

The bilinear nonlinearity `B(u,u) = (u·∇)u` produces Bohr coefficients
at sums:
   `B(u,u)_ζ = 2πi Σ_{ξ_1+ξ_2=ζ} (a_{ξ_1}·ξ_2) a_{ξ_2}`

Stationary NS `−Δu + (u·∇)u + ∇p = 0` after divergence-free projection
gives, for each `ζ ∈ ℝ³`:
   `4π²|ζ|² a_ζ + 2πi P_{ζ^⊥} Σ_{ξ_1+ξ_2=ζ} (a_{ξ_1}·ξ_2) a_{ξ_2} = 0`

For `ζ ∉ Σ`, `a_ζ = 0`, so symmetrizing:
   **`P_{ζ^⊥} [(a_{ξ_1}·ξ_2) a_{ξ_2} + (a_{ξ_2}·ξ_1) a_{ξ_1}] = 0`**
for every `ξ_1, ξ_2 ∈ BohrSpec` with `ξ_1 + ξ_2 = ζ ∉ Σ` and finitely-many
sum-pairs at `ζ`.

This is the **Bilinear Sum-Closure transversality constraint at leaked
sums**.

